                <head>339. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On December 13, elections for the offices of President and Vice President were
                    held by the Greek and Turkish communities. Archbishop Makarios was elected
                    President of the new republic and Dr. Fazil Kuchuk, running unopposed, was
                    elected Vice President. Belcher commented on the issues involved in the
                    elections in telegram 224 from Nicosia, November 27. (Department of State,
                    Central Files, 747C.00/11–2759) He analyzed the results of the elections in
                    telegram 256 from Nicosia, December 16. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>.,
                    747C.00/12–1659)</p>
            </div>
